From 07e9abf2dd88c08d22dc9202bd19e7d1609fc9e2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Project Luma <devnull@projectluma.local>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 12:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] window: adopt the native Luma application frame

Retain Text Editor's sessions, actions, adaptive property panel and editing
engine, but give those real controls the same application identity, command
row, work-surface boundary and window geometry as first-party Luma apps.

The application menu model moves to the identity trigger instead of being
duplicated. Open, New, fullscreen restoration and document properties remain
the existing widgets and actions; only their native composition changes.
